        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Joan of Arc</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1412 CE – 1431 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1412 (date unknown) in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/domremy-la-pucelle">Domrémy</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a> valley in north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>; daughter of Jacques d'Arc, a peasant farmer and village official, and Isabelle Romée</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">30 May 1431 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rouen">Rouen</a>, burned at the stake in the Vieux-Marché as a relapsed heretic, aged about nineteen; her remains were thrown into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seine">Seine</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val">Military leader with the Armagnac armies of Charles VII (1429–1430), without formal command; ennobled with her family by Charles in 1429; canonized in 1920 and declared a patron saint of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1922</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">the relief of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Orléans</a> in May 1429; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a> Campaign and the victory at Patay; the coronation of Charles VII at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reims">Reims</a>; her visions of Saint Michael, Saint Margaret and Saint Catherine; her trial for heresy and execution at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rouen">Rouen</a>; the rehabilitation trial of 1455–1456; her canonization in 1920</span></div>
        </div>
